#. type: Title #
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remote access (Tunnel + app token)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> When exposing the home PC Hub via **Cloudflare Tunnel**, Hub **`remote_auth`** Bearer token protects non-local connections.\n"
"> Security context: [`security.md`](security.md) · Install: [`install.md`](install.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer                 | Role                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| **Hub `remote_auth`** | Plaintext token in `config.yaml`; REST `Authorization: Bearer`; SAP `connect` frame `auth_token`; MCP `/mcp` same Bearer |\n"
"| **cloudflared**       | Outbound tunnel; Hub hostname → `127.0.0.1:2658`, Web hostname → `127.0.0.1:2659` (optional)                             |\n"
"| **Client settings**   | app/desktop / app/mobile / **browser Web** fill Hub URL and token in **Hub settings**                                    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:19
msgid ""
"Token is **skipped** only when **Host is loopback** (`127.0.0.1` / "
"`localhost` / `::1`) **and TCP peer is loopback** (local dev, CLI/systemd "
"health checks). Public domains (via Tunnel), LAN IPs, etc. require token; "
"independent of `tunnel.enabled`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Hub configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:23
msgid ""
"In `~/.anima/config.yaml` (**omit for local-only**; required before LAN or "
"public exposure):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"remote_auth:\n"
"  token: \"replace with openssl rand -base64 32 output\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:30
msgid "Generate:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "openssl rand -base64 32\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:36
msgid ""
"`.gitignore` ignores `config.yaml`; do not commit. Admin API redacts "
"`remote_auth.token` on read."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Tunnel (optional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"anima tunnel setup\n"
"anima service start\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:45
msgid ""
"When `tunnel.enabled: true`, cloudflared starts with **`anima service "
"start`** stack (no separate `anima-tunnel.service`). Ingress defaults to "
"local Hub `:2658`; with `tunnel.web_hostname` and `web.enabled`, second "
"ingress points to Web `:2659`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"tunnel:\n"
"  enabled: true\n"
"  hostname: anima.example.com\n"
"  web_hostname: app.anima.example.com\n"
"\n"
"web:\n"
"  enabled: true\n"
"  port: 2659\n"
"  public_url: https://app.anima.example.com\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without Tunnel, LAN clients use `http://<PC-IP>:2658` (Hub) and `:2659` (Web); fill Hub URL and token in client settings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cloudflare credentials (pass)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| pass path                                | Purpose                       |\n"
"| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n"
"| `services/cloudflare/api-token`          | Create Tunnel / DNS           |\n"
"| `services/cloudflare/tunnel-credentials` | `cloudflared` connector creds |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:68
msgid "See wizard `anima tunnel setup`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Client configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "**app/desktop**, **app/mobile**, and **browser Web** (`web.enabled` + Tunnel or LAN `:2659`) are remote clients; they **do not read** Hub `config.yaml` token.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Client      | Storage                                          |\n"
"| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| app/desktop | `~/.anima-desktop/settings.json` (`hub` section) |\n"
"| app/mobile  | Capacitor Preferences                            |\n"
"| Browser Web | localStorage (settings page)                     |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:80
msgid ""
"Desktop debug and Sentry config share the same file `debug` section; "
"override dir with `FREEANIMA_DESKTOP_HOME` (default `~/.anima-desktop`). "
"Legacy `~/.anima/shell-client.json` migrates on first launch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:82
msgid "Settings (all clients):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:85
msgid ""
"**Hub URL** — e.g. `https://anima.example.com` (when Web UI and Hub differ, "
"use **Hub** hostname, not Web UI domain)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:85
msgid "**Remote token** — same as Hub `remote_auth.token`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:87
msgid ""
"Browser Web: `/config.json` may suggest default Hub (`tunnel.hostname`); "
"first visit still requires saving token in settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:89
msgid ""
"Flow: open Hub settings → fill → **Test connection** → Save. Desktop "
"requires **restart app/desktop** after save."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Authentication behavior"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"REST:  Authorization: Bearer <token>\n"
"SAP:   WebSocket /sap/v1 → connect frame includes auth_token\n"
"MCP:   POST/GET /mcp → Authorization: Bearer <token>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. MCP outbound (external agents query Hub data)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:101
msgid ""
"Hub serves Streamable HTTP MCP Server at **`/mcp`**, exposing read-only "
"tools from ToolSets with `expose_mcp: true` (e.g. `memory_recall`, "
"`conversation_search`). External MCP clients (Cursor, Claude Desktop, etc.) "
"connect **without LLM relay**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# External agent example (Cursor mcp.json, etc.)\n"
"mcpServers:\n"
"  freeanima:\n"
"    url: http://127.0.0.1:2658/mcp\n"
"    headers:\n"
"      Authorization: \"Bearer <remote_auth.token>\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:114
msgid ""
"**Inbound** (Hub connects to external MCP servers): `config.yaml` "
"`mcp_servers` (`capabilities/mcp-client`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:114
msgid ""
"**Outbound** (external agents call Hub tools): `/mcp` endpoint "
"(`capabilities/mcp-server`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:114
msgid ""
"Public / LAN access requires same `remote_auth` token as REST; loopback may "
"omit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:116
msgid "Missing or wrong token → HTTP `401` or SAP connection closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:118
msgid ""
"Decision uses request URL **Host** (public domain via Tunnel, e.g. "
"`anima.example.com`) and **TCP peer**; Hub does not use `tunnel.enabled` to "
"decide token enforcement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:127
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Command                        | Description                                    |\n"
"| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `anima tunnel status`          | Tunnel / cloudflared status                    |\n"
"| `anima tunnel start` / `stop`  | Manual cloudflared (production: service stack) |\n"
"| `anima web start --foreground` | Standalone Web static server (debug)           |\n"
"| `anima service status`         | Hub / Web / Tunnel stack                       |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Symptom                | Check                                                                    |\n"
"| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Public 502             | Is Hub running? `anima service status`                                   |\n"
"| Public 1033            | `anima tunnel status` shows `connected: no`                              |\n"
"| 401                    | Client token matches `remote_auth.token`                                 |\n"
"| Local OK, remote fails | Remote requests need Bearer / SAP auth_token; public Host requires token |\n"
"| 401 after token change | Update Hub config **and** all client settings pages                      |\n"
msgstr ""

